Title: Historical Significance of Local Architecture
Exploring the local architecture in our town provides a fascinating insight into our cultural heritage. From Victorian homes with ornate trims to mid-century modern buildings, these structures tell a unique story of the people's values and aesthetics throughout the past centuries. The Historic Society is actively documenting and restoring significant structures that represent different periods of our town's development. Upcoming events include community walks, where locals can learn about the architectural features of various buildings and their historical contexts. It’s an opportunity to connect with our heritage and appreciate the artistry involved in our community’s growth.

